Robert Marenda wrote:
> Hello Everyone,

> Now for a question or two. When I find a wand, and I do not have a spare 
> scroll of identify, what are some safe ways to identify it? last time I 
> zapped a grid bug and discovered my wand was a wand of polymorph. This was 
> an effective way of identifying the wand but when the grid bug became a 
> raven, the game ended quite abruptly.

There is in fact an easy way to ID most wands. Engrave with them. That 
will use one charge, but most of the time it will at least give you a 
good clue what the wand does without much risk (a wand of create monster 
will still summon a monster though). For best results, write something 
in the dust with your finger (specify "-" for what to engrave with) 
first, as some wands require that there already be writing there.

> I have also been avoiding using fountains and sinks. I fear drinking from 
> fountains because I keep releasing nasties that kill me. I also have given 
> up on dumping rings down sinks to identify them. Any tips on when to (and 
> when not to) use fountains and sinks? 

Drinking from fountains can be very dangerous early on, but there's also 
a (small) change a water demon will appear and grant you a wish. So if 
you're level one and haven't invested much time in the character yet, 
you might consider that a risk worth taking.

Sinks, give more interesting stuff by kicking them than drinking from 
them. Kicking a sink may get you a ring (one per sink only), or cuase 
either a black pudding or a succubus (inccubus if you're female) to 
appear. Both of those monsters have some interesting properies.

